/*
 * BENCmouth GUI - Windows resources
 *
 * The icon lives here and only here. The CLI is a console program nobody
 * double-clicks, so giving bm.exe a 370 KB icon would be 370 KB spent on
 * something no one sees.
 *
 * The name matters. GLFW looks for an icon resource called exactly GLFW_ICON
 * when it registers the window class, and falls back to IDI_APPLICATION - the
 * generic Windows icon - when it does not find one. A numeric ID gives Explorer
 * the right icon while leaving the titlebar and taskbar generic, which is
 * exactly the half-working state this replaces.
 *
 * Explorer is happy either way: with one icon group in the binary, that is the
 * one it uses.
 */

GLFW_ICON ICON "assets/icon/bencmouth.ico"
